   "xml_index": 1,
   "xml_name": "PS4_001_DEBUG Discount For Kids And Seniors",
   "display_name": "Discount For Kids And Seniors",
   "questiontext_html": "<p><b>This is a DEBUG-TYPE question. Please read this carefully, it works differently from the other questions.</b></p>\n<p>The answer box below already contains a complete function. For the one example test shown below, this function gives the correct output.</p>\n<p><b>But the function has a logical mistake</b> (possibly more than one). For some other valid inputs, which we have <b>not</b> shown you, it gives a wrong answer or stops with an error.</p>\n<p><b>What you need to do:</b></p>\n<ol><li>Read the code carefully and trace it in your head for different valid inputs, to find the inputs where it goes wrong.</li><li>Fix the mistake(s), so that the function works correctly for <b>all</b> valid inputs described below.</li><li>Add a short comment in the code saying which line(s) you changed and why.</li></ol>\n<p><b>How this question is checked:</b> this question has some <b>hidden tests</b> that check exactly those inputs. When you click <b>Check</b>, we run your code on the example test and on the hidden tests. The pre-filled code will fail at least one hidden test; once you have fixed the mistake(s) correctly, all tests will pass.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><b>The function:</b> <code>gets_discount(age)</code> takes a person's age (a non-negative integer, int &gt;= 0) and <b>returns</b> <code>True</code> if the person gets a discount, or <code>False</code> if not. A person gets a discount if they are <b>younger than 12</b>, or if they are <b>60 or older</b>.</p>\n<p><b>Your fixed function must work for:</b> any non-negative integer <code>age</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Example test (already passes):</b> <code>gets_discount(30)</code> returns <code>False</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# The code below has a logical bug. It will not work correctly for some\n# valid inputs other than the one shown in the example.\n# Identify the BUG and CORRECT it. Add a comment saying what you changed.\n\ndef gets_discount(age):\n    if age < 12 and age >= 60:\n        return True\n    else:\n        return False\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(gets_discount(30))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "False",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(gets_discount(8))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "True",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(gets_discount(65))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "True",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(gets_discount(60))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "True",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    }
   ]
  },
