   "xml_name": "PS4_003_DEBUG Smallest Digit",
   "display_name": "Smallest Digit",
   "questiontext_html": "<p><b>This is a DEBUG-TYPE question. Please read this carefully, it works differently from the other questions.</b></p>\n<p>The answer box below already contains a complete function. For the one example test shown below, this function gives the correct output.</p>\n<p><b>But the function has a logical mistake</b> (possibly more than one). For some other valid inputs, which we have <b>not</b> shown you, it gives a wrong answer or stops with an error.</p>\n<p><b>What you need to do:</b></p>\n<ol><li>Read the code carefully and trace it in your head for different valid inputs, to find the inputs where it goes wrong.</li><li>Fix the mistake(s), so that the function works correctly for <b>all</b> valid inputs described below.</li><li>Add a short comment in the code saying which line(s) you changed and why.</li></ol>\n<p><b>How this question is checked:</b> this question has some <b>hidden tests</b> that check exactly those inputs. When you click <b>Check</b>, we run your code on the example test and on the hidden tests. The pre-filled code will fail at least one hidden test; once you have fixed the mistake(s) correctly, all tests will pass.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><b>The function:</b> <code>smallest_digit(n)</code> takes a positive integer (int &gt; 0) <code>n</code> and <b>returns</b> its smallest digit. For example, the digits of 382 are 3, 8 and 2, so the answer is 2.</p>\n<p><b>Your fixed function must work for:</b> any positive integer <code>n</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Example test (already passes):</b> <code>smallest_digit(507)</code> returns <code>0</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# The code below has a logical bug. It will not work correctly for some\n# valid inputs other than the one shown in the example.\n# Identify the BUG and CORRECT it. Add a comment saying what you changed.\n\ndef smallest_digit(n):\n    smallest = 0\n    while n > 0:\n        digit = n % 10\n        if digit < smallest:\n            smallest = digit\n        n = n // 10\n    return smallest\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(smallest_digit(507))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "0",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(smallest_digit(382))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "2",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(smallest_digit(9))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "9",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
